name: Message
type: Coordination/Event
description: >
  Base type for addressed, threadable communication between participants and
  documents. A Message may target a recipient channel, belong to a thread, and
  answer another Message. Requests, Responses, chat messages, operation
  requests, lifecycle messages, and document-emitted asks are all Messages, so
  one correlation model covers questions and answers, offers and counter-offers,
  asks and fulfilment, and free-form chat.

requestId:
  type: Text
  description: >
    Optional application-level correlation key. It may group retries, provider
    work, or multiple messages associated with one logical request. It is not a
    substitute for inResponseTo, which identifies an exact Message occurrence.

threadId:
  type: Text
  description: >
    Optional thread key grouping related Messages without requiring a consumer
    to walk an inResponseTo chain.

recipientChannel:
  type: Text
  description: >
    Optional channel key identifying the participant this Message is addressed
    to. When absent, the Message is addressed to the table as a whole or to the
    document itself. Addressing does not make a Message private; visibility
    follows the enclosing document and timeline rules.

# comment
inResponseTo:
  description: >
    Optional reference to the Message being answered, normally a pure
    { blueId: ... } reference to the exact Message occurrence or an equivalent
    materialized node. Any Message may answer any Message. Chains form a
    conversation tree; threadId provides direct grouping.
